course: dictionary
lesson: 14194
title: Motivated: keen, or having a reason
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Motivated has two main meanings. The first is keen and wanting to work hard. «Maya is very motivated, so she practises her spellings every night.» Maya wants to do well, so she works hard.
explain: The second meaning is caused by a reason. «The change of plan was motivated by the rain.» Here motivated tells you why the plan changed: the rain was the reason.
explain: Check the context. If the sentence is about a person working hard, motivated means keen. If it is about why something happened, motivated means it had a reason behind it. Try your meaning in the sentence to see if it fits.
fact: Motivated means keen and wanting to work hard to do something.
fact: Motivated also means caused or made to happen by a reason.
fact: «Motivated» is also the past form of the verb «motivate», which means to give someone a reason to act.
fact: «The thief was motivated by greed» means greed was the reason for the theft.
fact: A motivated pupil works hard in class, and a motivated athlete keeps training even when it is tiring.
exercise: «Sam is motivated, so he finishes every task before lunch.» What does motivated mean here? | Tired and sleepy | *Keen and wanting to work hard | Late for school | Lost in the playground
exercise: «The sudden price rise was motivated by a shortage of tomatoes.» What does motivated mean here? | Very hungry | *Caused by a reason | Happy and excited | Painted in bright colours
exercise: A school report says, «Ella was motivated all term.» What does this suggest? | *Ella worked hard and kept trying | Ella moved house | Ella was absent every day | Ella forgot her books
test: «The team was motivated by a big prize.» What motivated the team? | The school bus | The referee's whistle | The rain | *The prize
test: Which word means keen and wanting to work hard? | Barely | Treacherous | *Motivated | Curt
exam: Mr Khan says, «Your motivated effort shows in your work.» What does motivated effort mean? | Effort made by accident | Effort that is always too slow | *Effort that comes from wanting to work hard | Effort with no reason at all
